hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2690","**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakr, informed us Ibn Jurayj, who informed me Abu'z-Zubayr, that he heard Jabir ibn 'Abdullah say:

""We used to wear garments when we entered ihram that had not been touched by perfume or saffron. We used to wear al-mumashshaq garments, which were nothing but clay.""

Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' ibn Kurayb, narrated to us Zakariyya ibn 'Adiyy, from Ibrahim ibn Humayd, narrated to us Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, from Asma', who said:

""We used to cover our faces from men, and we used to do that before."""
